<h2>The design: why the corridor is sealed</h2>

<p>The Act\'s timeline discipline — 120 days outer limit for written statements, case management hearings, six-month trial windows, ninety-day judgment targets — would be fiction if every interlocutory order could detour to the High Court. Section 8 closes the revision route; Section 13(2) reinforces it by declaring that no appeal lies from any order or decree of a Commercial Division or Commercial Court otherwise than in accordance with the Act. Read together, the provisions channel all interlocutory grievances into two vessels: the short list of immediately appealable orders, and the appeal against the final decree for everything else.</p>

